The Viper project at ETH Zurich [1] provides a modern intermediate
verification language and suite of tools, designed for encoding a rich
variety of real-world verification problems down to a common set of core
primitives supported by Viper. These language primitives are designed
to encode a rich variety of reasoning principles and proof techniques
for different concrete programming settings. Viper is employed as a
back-end for verification tools targeting Java, Python, Rust, and OpenMP
code, to name a few.
